  "verdict": "The literature kernel is nearly a delta (centre voxel 0.829) yet its Wiener initialisation moves the missing voxels by 7.66e-02: missing-region MAE 0.05050 -> 0.09087 (+79.93 %), PSNR 23.485 -> 18.268 dB; DC gain 0.9524. After removing that DC factor the MAE is 0.10353 (+105.01 %), so the loss is not a brightness offset but amplified lattice-frequency artefacts (measured-region std 0.0654, 5.67 % of voxels above the reference maximum)."
